Lina (Design): Noticed a subtle UX/a11y bug on mobile: quick-swipe dismiss on toasts removes the toast before screen readers can announce the message or the undo action. Video attached from Pixel.
Noah (Frontend): Repro: on mobile density toolbar, perform an action -> toast slides in bottom-right -> user swipes it away quickly -> toast removed. On TalkBack sometimes the `aria-live` region never fires because the element is removed from DOM before announcement finishes.
Priya (a11y): That's expected behavior if DOM removal happens before SR announces. Two options: 1) delay unmount until `aria-live` finishes (tricky), 2) persist an offscreen live region copy for 600ms after removal, 3) disable swipe-to-dismiss for toasts with important context (eg. with undo). Prefer 2 + policy: important toasts opt-in for persistent announcement.
Marta (Mobile): On mobile we lean into gestures; disabling swipe by default might feel worse. Could we differentiate: swipable when toast is purely decorative (info), non-swipable when actionable (has undo/link). Also when user swipes, show an "Undo" affordance inline for 2s so they can restore.
Gus (Product): Product preference: keep gesture-first on mobile but never lose the ability to undo important actions. For destructive flows (delete dataset) we should show an undo in the toast that persists long enough. Also copy: make undo label explicit: 'Undo delete' vs just 'Undo'.
Noah (Frontend): Implementation idea: attach `data-actionable` attribute when toast has CTA/undo. UI: actionable toasts set `swipeable=false` and `aria-live=assertive` (if error) or polite (success). Non-actionable toasts remain swipeable and use polite live. For removal: when swiped, instead of immediate DOM removal, replace visible node with a lightweight `div role="status" aria-live="polite" class="sr-only">Message removed.</div>` for 700ms then remove. That lets SRs catch up.
Priya (a11y): Good start. A few more nits: 1) ensure the undo control is keyboard focusable and part of tab order; if toast is non-focusable for pointer-only flows, we still need a keyboard-accessible path (eg. move focus to banner or add a persistent crumb). 2) Don't rely solely on `sr-only` content; TalkBack on Android sometimes ignores elements that are visually hidden via CSS. Better to keep the live region offscreen but present. 3) Expose an API `toast.show({message, undoLabel, undoCallback, actionable:true})` so devs choose behavior explicitly.
Marta (Mobile): For native-like swipe, we'll animate height collapse and then replace with offscreen live node as Noah suggested. Also: if user swipes and undo appears, we can place an ephemeral snackbar at top of list with a single 'Undo' button focusable — that avoids trap inside a disappearing element.
Lina (Design): Visuals: prefer no pointer and a subtle shadow. For actionable toasts include a small inline CTA button "Undo delete" and set min-gap token 12px so they don't bump modal CTAs. For swipeable toasts we should show a small drag handle on hover to indicate gesture.
Noah (Frontend): Code sketch: 
```
const id = `toast-${Date.now()}`;
renderToast({id, text, actionable, undoLabel}){
  const el = document.createElement('div');
  el.id = id; el.setAttribute('role','status');
  el.setAttribute('aria-live', actionable? 'polite' : 'polite');
  el.dataset.actionable = actionable;
  el.innerHTML = `<span>${escape(text)}</span>${ actionable ? `<button class="toast-undo">${escape(undoLabel)}</button>` : ''}`;
  if(!actionable) enableSwipe(el);
}
function onSwipe(el){
  // replace with offscreen live copy for 700ms
  const sr = document.createElement('div');
  sr.className = 'sr-only'; sr.setAttribute('role','status'); sr.setAttribute('aria-live','polite');
  sr.textContent = `Removed: ${el.textContent}`;
  document.body.appendChild(sr);
  el.remove();
  setTimeout(()=> sr.remove(), 700);
}
```
Priya (a11y): A couple of suggestions: 1) use `aria-describedby` if toast references another element. 2) For undo, ensure the undo button has an accessible name like `button aria-label="Undo delete dataset ABC"` so assistive users know the target. 3) Add `prefers-reduced-motion` handling for swipe animations.
Gus (Product): Also request analytics: track `toast.swipe.dismiss`, `toast.undo.click`, `toast.auto.dismiss` to see how often users rely on undo. Could tie to product rules: if undo rate > 25% for a toast type, make it non-swipable by default.
Marta (Mobile): We'll implement initial PR that: - makes actionable toasts non-swipable, - keeps swipe for decorative toasts, - replaces removed toasts with offscreen live region for 700ms. Will add small top-snackbar undo fallback on mobile.
ci-bot: New PR opened: frontend#2759 - "toasts: swipe semantics + undo accessibility + live-region fallback"
Noah (Frontend): I'll add unit tests for `sr-preserve` and an integration test on Android emulator to ensure TalkBack reads the fallback node. Tagging @Priya for review. ETA: end of week.
Priya (a11y): Quick follow-ups: 1) document the new `actionable` flag in the component docs and include examples for common flows (delete, export, save), 2) provide a lint rule that warns when a toast with `actionable:true` has no focusable control.
Lina (Design): I'll update tokens and Figma frames: 1) min-gap 12px, 2) actionable toast shows inline CTA with 8px left margin, 3) add a small 16px drag handle indicator for swipeable toasts. Posting assets in #design-assets.
Gus (Product): Thanks team. Once PR lands let's monitor analytics for 2 weeks and iterate based on undo usage. :+1:
